if you're looking to grow your business  around the world by bringing on  international distributors I'm going to  share with you my five-step plan for how  to accomplish that hi I'm Evan  Carmichael  I believe in entrepreneurs and I  recently got a question from one of my  youtube viewers love you guys Adnan who  wrote in to say hey Evan I just started  watching your videos and I'm amazed  wonderful work Thank You Adnan I had a  question though I would like to know how  do you get in contact with international  agents like I live in a country where  readymade garments are the cheapest to  produce I'm looking for an agent who  could help me distribute and develop  countries like America where can I find  such contacts love this question Adnan  and as a quick little background on what  I've gone through my first business was  a software company I was based in  Toronto Canada and was struggling to get  sales and one of the things that really  helped me was negotiating deals with  international agents who could represent  our product it helped me go from making  $300 to get in my first five figure  check and then eventually being able to  sell in over 30 different countries so  here's the five-step process that I went  through that you can use to grow your  business number one is research  companies research is super easy to do  and you should be out there online  looking Google look on YouTube look on  social media for people who are  potential distributors for you an ideal  fit should be somebody who's already  selling different types of products to  your target market so when I was out  trying to find distributors from my  scientific software I was trying to find  people who are already selling to  scientists because that was the market I  wanted to reach I didn't want to find  somebody who lived in the country I  wanted to get into but had no experience  in the area and tried to convince them  to try to sell my scientific software  instead I looked for the companies who  already were selling to them and had  complementary products and services but  weren't direct competitors so start by  making that list of companies who's  already selling complementary products  and services to what you have to offer  and we'd see adding your product as a  value add to put through their chain  number two is create a deck  want to create an overview of your  company to show how reputable you are  there's a big fear in dealing with new  companies that maybe you're going to  fold after a couple of months maybe  you're going to take my money and run  that you're not going to stick around so  you want to show that you have  credibility and authority you want to  make sure you have a website that looks  legitimate and you create a PowerPoint  file or PDF that you can send them  showing as much credibility as possible  show how long you've been around for  show how many customers you have show  what media you've been in any anything  that you can share that makes me feel  like it's a safe bet going with you  instead of just gambling on some new  startup don't you show them the  opportunity that they have working with  you reduce their risk by showing the  credibility that you have any time  somebody's evaluating proposal they're  going to look at risk and then a look at  reward and too many times entrepreneurs  focus only on bumping up that reward but  if there's high risk the person is going  to say no so you have to increase the  reward and reduce the risk as much as  possible so create an amazing deck  number three is reach out with momentum  so you've made your list of all the  people you want to get in touch with you  created an amazing website and an  amazing deck to wow them now you want to  reach out to them introduce yourself but  have momentum behind you you don't want  to look desperate you don't want to make  it look like you're you're struggling  and this is your last chance at becoming  successful the way I reached out with  momentum to my potential distributors  was finding companies who already were  interested in our product that lived in  their country so when I approached the  potential distributor agent in Japan I  would show them all the results we  already had from Japan I would show them  that people were visiting our website  from Japan the people were downloading  the free demo of our product from Japan  that we had some customers from Japan  and I would say hey we have all this  opportunity coming from the Japanese  market and we don't know what to do with  it we'd love to partner with a local  expert who can really take this and run  so if you don't have customers yet then  show inquiries or show leads if you  don't have leads yet then show web  traffic if you don't have web traffic  from that country then go and get some  web traffic from that country you got to  show that you have some  momentum there so that you're reaching  out from a position of strength and not  despair and weakness number four is  discuss terms once you get in a call  with them and they learn about your  business they're going to want to know  what kind of terms are they going to get  how much is it going to cost them  what kind of commissions are they going  to get from it are you going to be  funneling them leads or not I'm going to  share with you three of the key terms  that I look for in every single  agreement that I made the first was  having an opt-out clause which meant  that within 30 days if I wasn't happy  with what they were doing I could cancel  on them and not owe them any more money  the second was a jurisdiction which  means if there's ever a conflict as if  there's ever a disagreement if there's  ever an opportunity that you might go to  court you're always governed by your  local laws so it always be governed  under the laws of Ontario Canada where I  was from and if we had to fight them  they would have to come to our courts to  fight us and number three is exclusivity  which meant they were the only ones to  potentially represent us in their  country if you deal with non-exclusive  then I would give them between 25 and 30  percent commission for every product  they sold for us but it also let me  negotiate with other people in their  country where if it was exclusive I  would give them 40 percent of every sale  that we made and it would be the only  person that would be allowed to sell in  their country  we'd also funnel them lead so that if we  got somebody from our website asking us  from their market then I would send them  the lead instead of trying to close them  myself and in general made a whole lot  of sense having people local on the  ground because I don't understand the  Japanese market I don't understand the  Japanese language I don't want to wake  up in the middle of the night to be able  to talk to a Japanese customer I'd much  rather have somebody local take care of  that for me  we also required our exclusive  distributors to purchase prepaid  inventory in advance so the first deal I  made was for 13 and a half thousand  dollars with a distributor in the UK it  was an exclusive arrangement where they  would take 40 percent commission on  everything sold and nobody else  represent us in the UK market and they  pre purchased thirteen and a half  thousand dollars worth of our software  that we would the dark as they started  making sales so know what terms you  in advance of going into that meeting  with them number five start a trial it  takes time for a company to get to know  your products and services and be able  to represent you really well it also  takes time for you to train them and  educate them and work with them on the  process so they can really represent you  that the best that they can in their  market so start with a three-month trial  train them work with them funnel them  leads if that's part of your deal make  sure that they understand who you are  what you're all about and are doing  their best possible job to represent you  you'll find quickly that some people are  really dedicated really motivated and  are moving a lot of product for you and  others you'll find talker with a good  game but then don't actually deliver any  results so keep the ones that are doing  well up to the trial and fire the ones  who art so that's my five-step process  to getting international distributors  that work for me I had a lot of success  with it and I hope that it works for you  as well believe for those of you  watching like the video you want to see  more like it  you can subscribe to the channel and let  me know what you think if you have a  question in the comments below thank you  so much for watching and I'll see you  soon self-improvement books are like  Fitness books they never work on their  own what you need is a trainer that's  Evan gap the newsletter  you

